WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.460
Chirico, you still haven't recovered yet.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.380
You can't fight them head-to-head and win!

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.210
There's no other way!

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:06.960
No! It'll be easier for me to cover you
if we spread out.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.170
Right...

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:11.130
The way things are now, they'll kill us both!

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.920
Surely you see that!

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:18.460
Don't forget, Chirico, we're fighting
so we can both live.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:23.540
Showdown

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:31.630
Chirico!

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.710
This is unusual.

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:27.920
What?

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:31.540
Ypsilon's Emotion Index is
falling to very low levels,

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.710
even though he's close to
the moment of killing Chirico.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.040
It's hatred.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:40.540
Fully born hatred ceases to be emotional.

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:44.880
The urge to kill your opponent
becomes one of cold-blooded logic.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:50.670
Chirico's quite a man to have
driven Ypsilon to this point.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:53.750
I want a full analysis on Ypsilon when this is over.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.080
But only after we've done our duty.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:57.880
It's starting.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.420
Damn you!

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.790
Chirico! Are you all right?

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:47.170
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.130
Get inside the ship! I'll need your help in there!

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:51.380
Inside?

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.960
I'm going to lure Ypsilon in front of
the main engine nozzle.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.210
Stand by in the control room! Go!

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:57.000
Chirico!

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.290
Capture Proto One!

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:08.710
We still need her! Don't kill her!

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.420
This will be your graveyard!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.920
Chirico! I'm all set!

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.500
Can you see me?

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:30.290
Yes, I see you.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:32.380
Chirico, are you in pain?

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:34.380
No, I'm fine.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.130
This is a question of timing. Get ready!

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:56.500
Let's go!

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:05.880
Now! Do it!

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:06.830
Ypsilon!

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:07.830
Hurry!

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:31.960
Y-Ypsilon...

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.290
Forgive me!

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:38.460
Is Ypsilon...?

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:40.000
We still read life signs.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.460
Recover him, quickly!

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:43.670
Recover Ypsilon at once!

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:44.960
What about Chirico?

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:47.750
You think you can beat him?!
All units, return to ship!

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:05.630
The other unidentified ship has ceased its attack.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.250
That's all we know.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:11.630
The ship that was forced down
fired its engines, but didn't take off.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.630
What's going on down there?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:20.210
What we know for sure is that ships are
fighting in a cease-fire zone.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:24.790
If we attack as well, the political reprecussions
would be disastrous.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:28.500
Send as many ships as we can
disguise into the area.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:29.250
And then?

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:31.420
Have them observe from within firing range.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.880
They'll provoke an attack and take care of them.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:37.420
Gentlemen, this operation is vital.

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:41.130
The important question is
will the other one attack first?

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:43.580
Give the orders!

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:46.250
I want those ships en route inside of five hours!

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.040
Yes, sir!

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:01.540
Your skin's badly damaged,
but a silicone treatment will fix that.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:03.080
Nothing serious.

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:05.250
That wasn't the only damage.

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:08.290
The analysis equipment we had on him
was totally destroyed.

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:11.330
Can I go?

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:13.210
Your AT is being repaired.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.750
Don't embarrass us
any more than you already have.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:19.330
If you keep wrecking yourself so easily,
we'll never get anywhere.

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:30.540
Don't be so eager, Ypsilon.

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:49.000
Blood adrenaline level: Check.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.630
Acetylcholine level: Check.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:12:01.670
Incredible. No normal man can heal this fast!

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.540
Chirico!

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:12.670
Where are you, Chirico?

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:34.880
Chirico, what are you doing?! You have to sleep!

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:36.040
I'm fine.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:39.920
You're hurt. You won't recover fully unless you rest.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:43.420
I'm doing the port wing nozzles next.

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:45.920
I found some acetylene welders. Help me out.

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:02.330
Okay, open the valve.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:06.000
Chirico!

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:12.210
Chirico!

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:40.460
Chirico...

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.710
Chirico, what's wrong?

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:50.670
Chirico, are you all right? Chirico!

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:54.250
I remember where we are.

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:56.830
This planet is called Sunsa.

00:13:57.630 --> 00:14:00.460
There used to be a magnificent city here.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:02.790
Horrible battle.

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:05.380
So many people were killed.

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:12.040
Somebody who knows my past
put me on this ship and brought me here.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.250
Chirico!

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:15.630
I always thought I was just a normal soldier.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.670
Stop it, Chirico!

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:18.960
Forget it!

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.960
They want you to remember-

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:21.960
They're coming!

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:52.290
Here they come.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:54.920
Keep track of them on that monitor.

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:55.790
Right.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.330
Stay away from the main engine!

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.250
And remember, when you find them, attack!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.460
The girl, too?

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:06.420
Yes!

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:16.330
What happened?!

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:17.830
The vernier thrusters!

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.040
They've been modified!
They're incredibly powerful now!

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:22.380
I don't care how you do it, just get inside!

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:30.290
Number ten, port.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:39.170
It works. We've got 45 nozzles to work with,
but expect some to get in.

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:40.790
Number thirty-six, starboard.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.000
Number twenty-five, port.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:50.000
Number thirty-five, port.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:53.960
Shit!

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:04.040
Chirico's rigged their verniers as a weapon!

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:05.380
Tell them to hurry!

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:06.040
Yes, sir!

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:07.290
Stubborn fellow, isn't he?

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.790
But it's only a matter of time.

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:11.380
What is it?!

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:12.580
Ships approaching!

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:13.380
What?!

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:20.670
They aren't breaking off!

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:22.330
Five of them, unidentified!

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:23.670
They have to be Balarant.

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:25.830
This is a cease-fire zone!

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:29.830
They may be coming
because we're attacking Chirico.

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:33.040
They may use that as a pretext
to attack us for "security reasons."

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:35.710
Captain, we have to withdraw!

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:37.210
Captain!

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:39.630
Battle stations!

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:52.000
Any closer and we'll be vulnerable.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.130
Never mind. We're trying to
provoke them, remember?

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:04.460
All ships have opened their gunports.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.040
Contact Ypsilon!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:06.960
No!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:07.920
What?

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.040
He's working right now.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.080
They're taking battle positions.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.500
That's definitely a Balarant formation.

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:20.630
Listen, when we go into the shadow of
that wreckage, match speeds with it. Hide us!

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:25.790
The enemy ship's dead angled!

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.710
Keep taking us in.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:31.250
Remember, we're trying to
provoke them, so don't fire first!

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:42.080
All right, that's it. That's it... Take it slow...

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:46.380
Right! When I give the word, pop up!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:49.710
Now!

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:56.960
Thermal reaction near the wreckage!
Approaching rapidly!

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:59.670
Don't panic! Continue observation.

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:03.790
Remember, don't fire unless they fire first!

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:11.330
Dorsal thrusters! Take us into
the shadow of the wreckage!

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:16.000
I don't care if you hit or not! Just cut them off!

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:24.750
Return fire, all units! It's only one ship!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:33.670
Do you have Ypsilon yet?

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:34.790
I've got him on line now!

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:36.920
Take us back into the wreckage!

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:48.080
Sir! Message from the Teltain!

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:52.420
This is the captain! We're under Balarant attack!

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:53.670
Return to ship!

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:56.000
But we just got in here!

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.420
Return to ship!

00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.330
In a moment, sir!

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:08.540
A lot of them have gotten in.
Chirico, we're in trouble!

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:10.380
We'll abandon ship.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.420
I have a plan.

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:51.750
Looks like Chirico's rigged something.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:54.040
Take it!

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:03.630
It's on self-destruct!
We have one minute to escape!

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:06.330
This is the hangar! It's Chirico! He's-

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:11.040
Get in the trailer.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:11.830
Right!

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.960
We'll roll out when we hear the first explosions.

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:47.170
Come on, move it!

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.040
It's started!

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:54.920
Let's go!

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.880
The Balarant are hanging
just outside our firing range.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:20.670
They don't seem to be attacking.

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:21.880
Damage report.

00:21:22.290 --> 00:21:24.830
We're still checking that. We took a pounding, sir.

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:27.080
This is all Ypsilon's fault.

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:28.420
That's not true.

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:33.040
You let the Balarant provoke you.
This is your responsibility.

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:34.420
Quite.

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:03.040
Well, we finally got off that ship.

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:07.830
And you've recovered in an amazingly short time.

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:10.750
Now we really are alone.

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:12.580
I doubt that.

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:27.130
Would we ever have any peace?

00:22:27.880 --> 00:22:30.080
I felt like screaming.

00:22:31.670 --> 00:22:35.710
If there was a God on this world,
he was a cruel one.

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:37.210
Too cruel.

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:41.420
This planet's name is Sunsa.

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:44.380
And I know...

00:22:45.250 --> 00:22:48.080
I know it holds no welcome for me at all.

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.250 --> 00:22:58.960
Red sky. Red earth.

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:02.330
All dyed red by an immeasurable amount of blood.

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:03.500
A cursed planet.

00:23:04.170 --> 00:23:07.880
One bearing the scars of the Red Shoulders,

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:12.670
the Melkian Strategic AT Special Ops
Corps X-1's, violent mission.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:16.170
Next time, "Planet Sunsa"

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:21.290
On this world, steel devils with
crimson shoulders once rampaged.

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.290
Planet Sunsa

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Whenever I'm alone

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Whenever I long for you

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Brighter than any other light...
